      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BENEFICIARY (4) is a lightly tried 6YO gelding with a terrific record, scoring 5 times from 7 starts. He has had 3 tune-up trials, and with top hoop Anthony Darmanin picking up the ride for the first time, he is the one to beat fresh up. COAL RIVER (2) has been freshened up since a modest effort at Devonport-synthetic just over 8 weeks ago as the favourite. He looked back to his best when winning a recent trial, and from a handy gate, he can make amends. Follow your money. SHY GUY (3) turned his form around when winning his penultimate start on the poly surface at Devonport and then was just fair here 2 weeks ago over 1400m, which was too short for him. He is worth another chance over a mile, so stick with him. THICKSKINNED (8) stepped up to this trip last start and bolted in by over 2 lengths. He drops 5kg, so go again.",
